login - start a console session

SYNOPSIS
    login

DESCRIPTION
    Read a login name and password at the console. Password input is hidden.
    On success, enter the user's home directory, print the message of the
    day and start the shell with the user's IDs. Rejected sign-ins are
    delayed.

    On a fresh data disk, the startup login prompts for a root password
    before accepting the first sign-in.

FILES
    /etc/motd    Message printed at sign-in.

SEE ALSO
    id(1), passwd(1), sh(1), useradd(1)
